


This dataset comprises four sets of fastq files.

These data were generated by sequencing a mock community (e.g. a sample of DNA created by adding known ququantities of DNA from a collection of different species).

In some of these samples (Even), the same amount of DNA is added from every species.

In other samples (staggered), different amounts of DNA are added from different species.

"Processed" means that the fastq file has been quality controlled with the software "Trimmomatic" by the sequencing provider.

"Raw" means that the fastq has not been quality-controlled.

"Raw Even" and "Processed Even" are exactly the same sequencing data, except that the latter has been quality controlled by the sequencing provider.

The same is true for "Raw Staggered" and "Processed Staggered".


Key to data:
PE = processed even
PS = processed staggered
RE = raw even
RS = raw staggered


